{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795461835,"nonce":"x5BBd1rYeT4i8c9J/X3DO6F3PcE=","title":"jno.fvm: a steady solve with a traced or missing x0 probes its Jacobian pattern at zeros, where a gas has no state","message":"Found on feat/fvm while fixing 57216bf (fc0394ff fixed the same probe for marches). _steady_solve decides the sparsity pattern at probe_at = zeros when x0 is None or traced (jno/_fvm/trace.py, the steady branch: \"m/rho is undefined at 0\"). A steady participant in a coupling is always in that case: _StrongForm.solve jits its solve with x0 traced, starting from zeros. For a gas the check then fails as the march did (complex wave speeds at the noise state). A march now probes at its initial state; a steady problem has none, so it needs a concrete state from the caller (the first warm start, an x0 given at build time) or the pattern decided eagerly before the solve is compiled. Related: 085dc18 (the coupling stiffness probe of a steady side from zero).","files":null}]}